From: BerryMC <148406068+BerryMC@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:02:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid cloning the direction values array for random
 directions

EnumDirection.a(Random) called values() twice per invocation, cloning
the static direction array twice for one random pick. Use the cached
EnumDirection.n array (same contents and order, filled once in the
static initializer) instead. Based on Leaf's 'Lithium fast util'
direction optimization.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/EnumDirection.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/EnumDirection.java
index cf3db56cfea38b8d5eab40286810579c91cc836d..f72e1c2e367ef01806a13d04de030f1a023d3a74 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/EnumDirection.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/EnumDirection.java
@@ -133,7 +133,9 @@ public enum EnumDirection implements INamable {
     }
 
     public static EnumDirection a(Random random) {
-        return values()[random.nextInt(values().length)];
+        // Dionysus start - pick from the cached array instead of cloning the values() array twice per call
+        return EnumDirection.n[random.nextInt(EnumDirection.n.length)];
+        // Dionysus end
     }
 
     public String toString() {
